# Ride Optimizer - Smart Static Architecture Cron Jobs
# Replace PROJECT_PATH with actual path to project root
# Replace CONTAINER_NAME with the running podman container name
#
# Jobs run inside the app container via `podman exec` instead of with the
# host's own Python. data/ and config/ are bind-mounted into the container
# and owned by its rootless-Podman subuid, not the host cron user — running
# the scripts on bare host Python caused near-constant PermissionError
# failures on every job (#543). `podman exec` runs as the container's
# default user (rideopt), which already owns those files.

# Daily analysis at 2 AM
0 2 * * * cd PROJECT_PATH && podman exec CONTAINER_NAME python cron/daily_analysis.py >> logs/cron.log 2>&1

# Weather refresh every 6 hours
0 */6 * * * cd PROJECT_PATH && podman exec CONTAINER_NAME python cron/weather_refresh.py >> logs/cron.log 2>&1

# Cache cleanup daily at 3 AM
0 3 * * * cd PROJECT_PATH && podman exec CONTAINER_NAME python cron/cache_cleanup.py >> logs/cron.log 2>&1

# System health check every other hour
0 */2 * * * cd PROJECT_PATH && podman exec CONTAINER_NAME python cron/system_health.py >> logs/cron.log 2>&1

# Error-log triage weekly on Sunday at 3:30 AM — before rotation below wipes
# the logs it reads. Files (deduped, capped) GitHub issues for recurring
# ERROR/WARNING clusters in logs/cron*.log; runs inside the container so it
# can reuse src/pii_sanitizer for redaction. See scripts/log-triage.sh.
30 3 * * 0 cd PROJECT_PATH && ./scripts/log-triage.sh >> logs/cron_log_triage.log 2>&1

# Log rotation weekly on Sunday at 4 AM. Rotates unconditionally regardless
# of mtime — the old `find -mtime +7` trigger never fired because these
# files are appended to as often as every 2 hours, so mtime never aged past
# 7 days (#545 / #553). See scripts/rotate-logs.sh.
0 4 * * 0 cd PROJECT_PATH && ./scripts/rotate-logs.sh

# Weekly maintenance (docs/issue hygiene, backups, worktree pruning) — Sunday at 5 AM.
# Runs as host bash directly, not podman exec: it needs git/gh/jq against the
# host checkout itself, not the containerized app's bind-mounted data/config.
# AUTO_COMMIT_MAINTENANCE=true is what makes this unattended run auto-commit
# and push ISSUE_PRIORITIES.md/the maintenance log — see
# docs/releases/maintenance/WEEKLY_MAINTENANCE.md. Requires GH_TOKEN in .env.
0 5 * * 0 cd PROJECT_PATH && AUTO_COMMIT_MAINTENANCE=true ./scripts/weekly-maintenance.sh >> logs/cron_weekly_maintenance.log 2>&1
